SUMMARY:In The Other Room: Adam Cayton-Holland
LOCATION:Helium Comedy Club\, 3070 Windward Plaza\, Portland
DESCRIPTION:Adam Cayton-Holland is a nationally touring comic who has appea
 red on  Conan \,  Corden \,  Comedy Central \, and a bunch of other grea
 t stuff that starts with the letter "C."\n\nAlong with his cohorts in the c
 omedy troupe\, The Grawlix\, he created\, wrote\, and starred on the TV sho
 w\,  Those Who Can't\,  which aired for three seasons. The Grawlix also h
 ost the longest running indie comedy show in the country in their home town
  of Denver\, and have a popular podcast called\, "Advice Fight.”\n\nAdam 
 has seven albums you can listen to wherever you do that sort of thing\, as 
 well a special\,  Wallpaper \, currently streaming on Hulu\, and another s
 pecial\,  20 Years In Comedy and All I Got Was This Lousy Special \, strea
 ming on YouTube.\n\nHis memoir\, Tragedy Plus Time\, is available everywher
 e\, and Adam recently adapted that book into the movie  See You When I See
  You \, for which he wrote the screenplay.\n\nThere is a two-item per perso
 n minimum in the Showroom\, which can be fulfilled with any food or drink i
 tems from the menu.\n\nPLEASE NOTE: Food and drinks purchased in the bar an
 d lounge do not count towards the two-item minimum.\n\nManagement reserves 
 the right to prevent customers from entering the facility who they deem dis
 ruptive or dangerous to other patrons.\nMore info: https://comedyatlas.app/
